W2 item 3b — CFI over an ASYMMETRIC base (does the item-3a counting bound survive?)
  item 3a's bound  reps >= |Aut-block| / |gauge-orbit| >= 2  needs Aut > gauge.
  Aut(CFI(G)) > gauge exactly when the BASE has automorphisms. All four item-3a
  witnesses had |Aut(base)| = 12, 12, 24, 12.  Here Aut(base) = 1.
  Every gauge element is verified edge-by-edge before use (same as item 3a).

=== 1. control: a SYMMETRIC base, to reproduce item 3a's verdict ===
  CFI over K4  (|Aut(base)|=24)  n=28  m=4  |E|=6  beta=3  |gauge|=8
     base: |Aut(base)|=24  degrees=[3, 3, 3, 3]  1-WL classes=1/4 ⟹ base is COARSE under 1-WL
     cell 0 (TARGET) [gadgets] |cell|=16  gauge-orbits=4  Aut-blocks=1  ⟹ ⛔ (B) NO block is one gauge-orbit — no key can fire it
     cell 1 [wires] |cell|=12  gauge-orbits=6  Aut-blocks=1  ⟹ ⛔ (B) NO block is one gauge-orbit — no key can fire it
     ⟹ non-singleton cells: 2   ✅ fire-today 0   ◐ key-limited 0   ⛔ blocked 2

